  "overview": {
    "title": "Mazagan as a whole",
    "p1": "The Portuguese City — still often called Mazagan — is the fortified heart of El Jadida and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Ramparts, gates, the cistern and the dense streets inside form one ensemble.",
    "p2": "Treat it as a walkable district rather than a single monument. Start at the cistern, climb to the Bastion of the Angel, then lose an hour in the lanes.",
    "p3": "This is Atlantic fortress heritage, not inland medina fantasy: stone, wind and sea define the mood."
  },
